<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏpīmo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		opimus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to fatten</i>, <i>make fat</i>
			(post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turtures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 7, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">8, 9,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Of the soil, <i>to make fruitful</i>, <i>to
			fertilize</i>: terram, App. de Mundo, p. 68,
			6.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>To enrich</i>, <i>to make rich</i> or
				<i>abundant</i>, <i>to fill</i>, <i>load</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auctumnum, Pomona, tuum September opimat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ecl. de Mensib. 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to honor</i>, <i>glorify</i>: numina victimis, Mart. Cap.
			poët. 9, § 914.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To enrich</i>, Aus. Ep.  15,
			1.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏpīmātus</span></b> , a,
			um, P. a., <i>fat</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abdomen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 10, 105</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
